drm/panel: himax-hx83112b: select DSI video mode

The HX83112B panel is configured for burst-mode video traffic, but its mode
flags omit MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO. The MSM display stack therefore classifies the
interface as command mode and selects command-mode completion paths. On the
Fairphone 3 that causes atomic state swaps to block and presentation to
phase-lock between 30 and 60 frames per second.

Set the base video-mode flag alongside the burst-mode modifier so the host and
display backend use the video-mode timing and completion paths.

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx83112b.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx83112b.c
index 263f79a967de..a882a1842600 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx83112b.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx83112b.c
@@ -376,7 +376,7 @@ static int hx83112b_probe(struct mipi_dsi_device *dsi)
 
 	dsi->lanes = 4;
 	dsi->format = MIPI_DSI_FMT_RGB888;
-	dsi->mode_flags = MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO_BURST |
+	dsi->mode_flags = MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO | MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO_BURST |
 			  MIPI_DSI_CLOCK_NON_CONTINUOUS |
 			  MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO_NO_HSA | MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM;
 
